%N A396731 Triangle read by rows: T(n,k) = A181187(n,k) + A138785(n,k), 1 <= k <= n.
%C A396731 Consider an arrangement of numbers A(n,k) with A000070(n) rows and n columns. The arrangement has two zones. The upper zone (or zone of partitions) contains the partitions of n. There is a partition of n per row, hence the upper zone has A000041(n) rows. The order of the partitions does not matter. The lower zone (or zone of divisors) contains the divisors of the numbers from the n-th row of the triangle A176206, with the divisors k in the column k, hence the lower zone has A000070(n-1) rows. The arrangement shows the correspondence between parts and divisors because the arrangement has the property that the numbers in the upper zone are the same as the numbers in the lower zone but in distinct order. For a "links zone" between the upper zone and the lower zone see A338156. T(n,k) is the sum of all elements in the k-th column of the arrangement of n (see the example).
%e A396731 Triangle begins:
